To achieve this, you'll need to combine the Azure Speech Service for text recognition, some text processing to extract the required information, and FlaUI for UI automation. Here's a step-by-step approach to handle your scenario in C#:

1. First, install the required NuGet packages:
   - Microsoft.Azure.CognitiveServices.Speech
   - FlaUI.Core
   - FlaUI.UIA3 (or FlaUI.UIA2 if UIA3 doesn't work for your application)

2. Add the following using directives:

```csharp
using Microsoft.Azure.CognitiveServices.Speech;
using FlaUI.Core;
using FlaUI.Core.Tools;
using FlaUI.Core.WaitHandling;
using FlaUI.UIA3;
using System;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;
```

3. Create a method to recognize speech from the microphone:

```csharp
public static string RecognizeSpeech()
{
    var config = SpeechConfig.FromSubscription("YourSubscriptionKey", "YourServiceRegion");
    using var recognizer = new SpeechRecognizer(config);
    return recognizer.RecognizeOnceAsync().Result.Text;
}
```

4. Create a method to extract the required information (control name, click type) from the recognized text:

```csharp
public static (string ControlName, string ClickType) ExtractInfo(string text)
{
    var match = Regex.Match(text, @"^(?<ClickType>left|right|double) click on (?<ControlName>.+)$", RegexOptions.IgnoreCase);
    if (match.Success)
    {
        return (match.Groups["ControlName"].Value, match.Groups["ClickType"].Value);
    }

    throw new Exception("Unable to extract control name and click type from the recognized text.");

